The bug-fix commit `52fa0d5` is a near-direct revert of `8b21759`'s change to `ZNode.java`, confirming it as the source.

## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: 8b217592ce18bd392a54064140001b6ceef89bd4

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** I traced the history of `java/src/libbun/parser/ast/ZNode.java` with `git log -p --follow`. This showed only two commits ever touched the affected constructor line: the fix commit `52fa0d5` (changing `ParentNode.SetChild(this, ZNode._EnforcedParent);` → `this.ParentNode = ParentNode;`) and, immediately preceding it, commit `8b21759` which made the exact opposite change (`this.ParentNode = ParentNode;` → `ParentNode.SetChild(this, ZNode._EnforcedParent);`). The fix is a literal revert of that one line.

**(2) The introduced bug:** Commit `8b21759` was a broader refactor (also touching `ZBlockNode.java` and `ZDesugarNode.java`) that replaced direct `ParentNode` field assignments with calls to the `SetChild` helper method, presumably to centralize parent-child bookkeeping. Looking at `SetChild`'s implementation (`ZNode.java:104-109`):
```java
public final ZNode SetChild(ZNode Node, boolean EnforcedParent) {
    assert(this != Node);
    if(EnforcedParent || Node.ParentNode == null) {
        Node.ParentNode = this;
    }
    return Node;
}
```
`ParentNode.SetChild(this, ZNode._EnforcedParent)` invokes this method *on* the `ParentNode` object itself. If `ParentNode` (the constructor argument) is `null` — which is legitimate for root/synthetic nodes — this becomes a null-pointer dereference (`null.SetChild(...)`), whereas the original `this.ParentNode = ParentNode;` safely assigns `null` to the field.

**(3) Supporting evidence:** Several `ZNode` subclasses construct nodes with an explicit `null` parent, e.g. `super(null, null, 0)` in `PHINode.java`, `JoinNode.java`, `ZDefaultValueNode.java`, and `super(null, null)`/`super(null, null, N)` in `ZBooleanNode.java`, `ZSetNameNode.java`, `ZWhileNode.java`. Any of these construction paths would trigger a `NullPointerException` under the code introduced in `8b21759`, and the fix in `52fa0d5` directly restores the null-safe assignment.

I'm confident in this identification given the direct revert relationship and the concrete NPE mechanism, though I did not run the test suite to reproduce the crash live (read-only investigation as instructed).

